{%- comment -%}
The lunr corpus, replacing Pagefind's binary index (plan §8).

Pagefind ran over the built `dist/`, so it indexed rendered HTML. Here the docs
are markdownified and stripped, which is the same text by the time it reaches the
index — lunr stems tokens, so markup residue would only add noise.

Scope: the docs collection, the three standalone docs pages, and the four
content pages. The 60 language and 6 style pages are deliberately excluded — they
render the same homepage section stack, so any homepage term would return 66
near-identical hits and bury the docs. See open item 13.

`description` is indexed alongside the body because three pages —
`/`, `/viewers/` and `/docs/inspect/` — carry no page content at all: their text
lives in the `home` layout's section includes. Pagefind indexed the rendered HTML
and so covered them; front matter is the closest equivalent Liquid can reach.

`jsonify` handles the escaping, including the backticks and quotes that appear
throughout the docs.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign extra_urls = "/,/about/,/osm2vectortiles/,/viewers/,/docs/,/docs/schema/,/docs/inspect/" | split: "," -%}
[
{%- assign first = true -%}

{%- for doc in site.docs -%}
  {%- unless first -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- assign first = false -%}
  {%- assign body = doc.content | markdownify | strip_html | normalize_whitespace -%}
  {"url":{{ doc.url | relative_url | jsonify }},"title":{{ doc.title | jsonify }},"category":{{ doc.category | jsonify }},"description":{{ doc.description | default: "" | jsonify }},"body":{{ body | jsonify }}}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- for url in extra_urls -%}
  {%- assign match = site.pages | where: "url", url | first -%}
  {%- if match -%}
    {%- unless first -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- assign first = false -%}
    {%- assign body = match.content | markdownify | strip_html | normalize_whitespace -%}
    {"url":{{ match.url | relative_url | jsonify }},"title":{{ match.title | jsonify }},"category":{{ match.category | default: "" | jsonify }},"description":{{ match.description | default: "" | jsonify }},"body":{{ body | jsonify }}}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]
